From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:14:47 +0300
Subject: renderergl2: no shadow and post-processing programs without
 framebuffer objects

Shadow maps, the sun's shadow mask, SSAO, tone mapping, bloom and the final copy to the screen all
draw into framebuffer objects, so without ARB_framebuffer_object (nv30 has none) their programs are
never bound: pshadow, down4x, bokeh, tonemap, calclevels4x (2), shadowmask, greyscale, ssao,
depthBlur (4), shadowfill (3, unless r_dlightMode >= 2) and the lightall shadow-map variants (18
with r_sunlightMode 1: upstream picks them without FBOs too, then samples a shadow mask that was
never made, its FIXME in RB_StageIteratorGeneric). Skip them when there are no FBOs and don't pick
the shadow-map variants then. r_glslAllPrograms 1 compiles them all again, as upstream.

The uniform setters also skip a program that was never built instead of writing through its NULL
uniform cache.

